,title,link,text,language,family
0,Riang language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riang_language,"Riang is a Palaungic language of Burma and China. Speakers are culturally assimilated with the Karen, but are Palaung by ancestry and their language is unrelated. Riang Lang and Riang Lai are sometimes considered distinct languages.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
1,Austroasiatic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austroasiatic_languages,"Among the Austroasiatic languages, only Vietnamese, Khmer, and Mon have lengthy, established presences in the written, historical record. Only two are presently considered to be the national languages of sovereign states: Vietnamese in Vietnam, and Khmer in Cambodia.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
2,Riang Lai / Yinchia - Max Planck Society,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Riang-Lai.htm,"Yinchia or Riang Lai has a decimal system similar to that of Riang. Tthousand is a loanword from Shan. Tone marksː a˦ = High tone, a˧ = Mid tone, a˧˥= High falling tone and a˥˩= Falling tone.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
3,Riang Ria Hari Raya - Playlist - Apple Music,https://music.apple.com/sg/playlist/riang-ria-hari-raya/pl.3aabbb24392247efa1e146becab09149,"Riang Ria Hari Raya Whether young or old, this Hari Raya medley of new hits and classics is perfect for the whole family.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
4,Austro-Asiatic etymology : List with all references,https://starlingdb.org/cgi-bin/etymology.cgi?root=config&basename=/data/aas/aaet&text_number=182&single=1,"Austro-Asiatic etymology : Search within this database Proto-Austro-Asiatic: *pi:jh Meaning:sweep Proto-Pearic:*phi:t.N Proto-Palaungic:*pilh aaet-meaning,aaet-pear,aaet-pawa,",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
5,Yinchia-Riang Lai - Max Planck Society,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Riang-Lai+-Yinchia.htm,"Other comments:Yinchia or Riang Lai has a decimal system similar to that of Riang. Tthousand is a loanword from Shan. Tone marksː a˦ = High tone, a˧ = Mid tone, a˧˥= High falling tone and a˥˩= Falling tone.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
6,A phonological analysis of Riang Lang | SIL Global,https://www.sil.org/resources/archives/81979,"Riang is a tonal language belonging to the Palaungic branch of the Austroasiatic languages. Based on new data, this paper presents a phonological description of a variety of Riang Lang, spoken in Namsang township of Shan State in Myanmar.",Riang Lai,Austro-Asiatic
